<Base title="About" description="TheCruxCo is a daily knowledge-first news digest for ambitious Indians.">
  <article class="container">
    <header style="padding-top:32px;">
      <span class="kicker">About</span>
      <h1>The crux of what matters. Every day.</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>TheCruxCo is a daily five-minute news digest built for people who want to think clearly about the next decade — not the next news cycle.</p>
      <p>Mainstream Indian news is loud. Western premium news is expensive. Most newsletters are either too thin or too specialized. TheCruxCo sits in the gap: seven categories, five items each, in under seven minutes, with a strict editorial rule against celebrity, gossip, political theatre, and outrage.</p>

      <h2>What we cover</h2>
      <p>Geopolitics and global affairs · Economy, business and markets · AI, technology and innovation · Health, medicine and biotech · Science and space · Society, law and culture · Future trends and big ideas. Every weekday morning, in the same shape.</p>

      <h2>What we don't cover</h2>
      <p>Celebrity news, entertainment gossip, influencer drama, social-media outrage, crime stories without broader significance, and political noise without long-term impact. If it won't matter in three years, it doesn't run.</p>

      <h2>Who writes it</h2>
      <p>The daily digest is curated by the editor. Weekly essays are written by paid human correspondents who publish under pen names — so the argument matters more than the byline. We disclose this openly; we do not publish AI-written essays as human work.</p>

      <h2>How it's free</h2>
      <p>TheCruxCo is funded entirely by display advertising, never by paywalls or subscriptions. No popups, no autoplay video ads, no content-recommendation widgets. Just a few well-placed units that pay for the work.</p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>Story ideas, corrections, sponsorship enquiries, or to write for us (anonymously) — <a href="/contact/">say hello</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
